#!/bin/bash

# ============================================================================
# Comprehensive Test Suite for MS-09 (Order Service — the checkout hub) v2.0
# Tests ALL 32 Business Rules (BR-ORD-001 to BR-ORD-032)
# ALL tests execute against the running service - ZERO SKIPS
# Generated by SAAM Framework
#
# NAMING AUTHORITY: spec/microservices/MS-09/04-api-contract.yaml (OpenAPI 3.1).
#   All paths, field names (snake_case, Concern A), status codes, envelopes, and
#   DECLARED headers come from the contract ONLY — never from 01-business-rules.md
#   Concrete Examples (those predate the contract and use camelCase).
#   Store scoping: x-store-id is REQUIRED (Concern B fix). x-store-id is a UUID
#   (spec/shared/infrastructure-patterns.md — malformed -> 400).
#
# ARCHITECTURE SEAMS (spec/microservices/MS-09/{01,02,05}-*):
#   BV-1/ADR-001  order OWNS the total; tax (MS-07) + shipping (MS-08) are sync
#                 stateless reads folded into the owned computation.
#   BV-2/ADR-003  order CONSUMES payment.captured / payment.refunded (idempotent on
#                 transaction_id). NO cross-service order write from payment. The
#                 contract exposes NO event-consumer HTTP endpoint, so the async
#                 settlement effect is exercised via the order's own refund endpoint
#                 (POST /{orderId}/refund) and asserted through the order read
#                 (INV-ORD-005/007 idempotent settlement).
#   D-08          checkout is a SAGA (charge -> persist -> publish order.placed) with
#                 an idempotency-key header, NOT 2PC.
#
# D-06 PRESERVE-FLAGGED rules (assessment/ba-decision-register.md — all Preserve-Flagged;
#   target neutralizes via architecture). Per the 4a disposition and the test brief:
#   BR-ORD-006  rounding: FIXED -> assert canonical 2dp HALF_UP rounding applied at the total layer.
#   BR-ORD-020  masked-PAN/CVV PCI: FIXED -> assert PAN is masked/tokenized, full PAN NEVER returned.
#   BR-ORD-032  download IDOR + unenforced limit: FIXED -> assert download requires ownership (403)
#               AND enforces the download-count/max-days limit.
#   BR-ORD-029  status assignment: PRESERVED -> free status assignment is allowed (unguarded set,
#               within the enum) per its D-06 flag.
#   BR-ORD-021  inverted pre-auth branch: preserved-and-flagged (behavior asserted at the seam).
#   BR-ORD-015  count/page filter-precedence divergence: preserved-and-flagged.
#   BR-ORD-031  integration channel bypasses payment/status orchestration: preserved-and-flagged.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPENDENCY MOCKS (05-dependencies.md — sync REST providers this service calls)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MS-09 depends on MS-01/03/04/05/06/07/08/10 (sync REST). The endpoints exercised
# below actually call the following; each is mocked (python3 http.server, in-process)
# returning contract-shaped responses from the provider's 04-api-contract.yaml:
#   - MS-07 tax      -> POST /api/v1/tax/calculate            (TaxCalculationResponse: tax_lines[])
#   - MS-08 shipping -> POST /api/v1/shipping/quotes          (ShippingQuote)
#                       GET  /api/v1/shipping/configuration   (ShippingConfiguration: handling_fees...)
#   - MS-10 payment  -> POST /api/v1/payments/process         (Transaction: transaction_id, event_published)
#                       POST /api/v1/payments/orders/{id}/capture
#                       POST /api/v1/payments/orders/{id}/refund
#   - MS-04 catalog  -> GET  /api/v1/catalog/products/{id}    (product snapshot: price/virtual/shippable)
#   - MS-05 customer -> POST /api/v1/customers | GET /api/v1/customers/{id}
#   - MS-03 store    -> GET  /api/v1/stores/{code}
#   - MS-01 reference-> GET  /api/v1/reference/... (fail-soft name lookups)
# Async events (payment.captured/refunded, order.placed) are NOT mocked as a broker —
# per the template they are integration-tested; here the settlement EFFECT is asserted
# through the order's refund endpoint + order read (BV-2 idempotent settlement).
# All dependency URLs are exported so the service under test resolves the mocks.
# ============================================================================

